act that shapes the entire acquisition thesis: Benny J. Stewart holds only **an undivided one-half (1/2) interest** in Lot 11, Block G/6041, as conveyed by General Warranty Deed recorded under Instrument No. **201700198338** in 2017. This is not a whole-lot play — it is a **fractional interest acquisition**, which immediately introduces a co-ownership complexity that must drive every decision in this memo. The 75233 zip code houses typically date to 1950–1965, placing this structure at approximately 60–75 years of age with meaningful physical depreciation. Brettonwoods homes in this corridor are predominantly single-story frame construction, 1,000–1,400 SF, on 6,000–7,500 SF lots. At this age and in this submarket, DCAD improvement values in comparable cases typically run **$45,000–$75,000** against land values of **$20,000–$35,000**, suggesting an improvement-heavy ratio of roughly 60–70% structure / 30–40% land. This makes it a **structure play with land optionality**, not a straight tear-down land hold — the structure carries usable rental or resale value if the deferred maintenance curve hasn''t gone terminal. The 2017 deed instrument date is significant: Stewart acquired his half-interest approximately 7–8 years ago, meaning he''s not a decades-long legacy owner, but he''s not a recent speculative buyer either. The fact that taxes only went delinquent in **2023 and 2024** — after years of presumably current payment — suggests a triggering event (job loss, health issue, death of co-owner, or financial disruption) rather than a chronic non-payer pattern. The **absence of prior related suits** in DC','\n',char(10)),'Standard Dallas County tax foreclosure case with typical LGBS representation and successful service','pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-12T14:33:24.445325','2026-07-09 05:11:41','2026-07-08T19:19:30.914511',1,'individual','high','ALL OF GRANTOR''S 1/2 INTEREST ONLY LOT 11, BLOCK G/6041, BRETTONWOODS, AN ADDITION IN THE CITY OF DALLAS, DALLAS COUNTY, TEXAS, AS SHOWN BY THE GENERAL WARRANTY DEED RECORDED AS INSTRUMENT NUMBER 201700198338 OF THE DEED RECORDS OF DALLAS COUNTY, TEXAS','{"account_number": "00008496024000000", "market_value": null, "land_value": null, "improvement_value": null, "estimated_annual_taxes": 0.0, "year_built": null, "effective_year_built": null, "actual_age": null, "building_class": "", "construction_type": "", "foundation": "", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": null, "total_area_sqft": null, "bedrooms": null, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": null, "desirability": "", "air_condition": "", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": null, "zoning": "", "lot_frontage_ft": null, "lot_depth_ft": null, "lot_area_sqft": null, "land_unit_price": null, "legal_description": "1: No Data 2: No Data 3: No Data 4: No Data 5: No Data Deed Transfer Date:", "owners": [], "deed_transfer_date": "", "exemptions": "None", "no_homestead": true, "tax_rates": [], "current_tax_balance": null, "current_levy": null, "prior_year_due": null, "payment_history": [], "tax_by_year": [], "distress": {"score": 4, "level": "high", "signals": [{"type": "no_homestead", "label": "No homestead exemption \u2014 not owner-occupied or absentee", "severity": "warning"}, {"type": "vacant", "label": "Improvement value near zero \u2014 likely vacant lot or demolished", "severity": "critical"}]}, "street_view_url": "https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/streetview?size=640x400&location=2822%20Larkspur%20Lane%2C%20Dallas%2C%20TX%2075233-3218&fov=90&key=AIzaSyD-placeholder", "dcad_url": "https://www.dallascad.org/AcctDetailRes.aspx?ID=00008496024000000", "act_url": "https://www.dallasact.com/act_webdev/dallas/showdetail2.jsp?can=00008496024000000&ownerno=0", "ownership_history": [], "owner_changes": [], "market_value_history": [], "taxable_value_history": [], "exemptions_history": [], "is_absentee": false, "estate_flag": false, "mailing_differs_from_property": false, "history_url": 