,7,0,1,'[]',1,0,1,'Multiple defendants unserved; Rule 106 substitute service granted for Refugio Ulloa and pending for Aranza Ponce; life estate situation with Jamie Cornejo','high','7 defendants with life estate and in rem claims; multiple unexecuted citations requiring Rule 106 substitute service (2 defendants); Citation by Posting affidavits filed for 3 defendants (Jamie Cornejo, Joel Uyoa, Jessica Ponce); ad litem appointments; estate/heir complications with life estate holder; 1 continuance and 1 trial reset',NULL,'none',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "DALLAS COUNTY", "taxAmt": 1532.55, "penaltyInterest": 932.87, "total": 2465.42}, {"entity": "DALLAS INDEPENDENT SCHOOL DISTRICT", "taxAmt": 6969.53, "penaltyInterest": 4269.03, "total": 11238.56}, {"entity": "CITY OF DALLAS", "taxAmt": 1151.13, "penaltyInterest": 700.04, "total": 1851.17}, {"entity": "PARKLAND HOSPITAL DISTRICT", "taxAmt": 319.84, "penaltyInterest": 194.19, "total": 514.03}, {"entity": "DALLAS COLLEGE", "taxAmt": 156.23, "penaltyInterest": 94.84, "total": 251.07}, {"entity": "DALLAS COUNTY SCHOOL EQUALIZATION FUND", "taxAmt": 0, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 0}]',replace('# ACQUISITION MEMO: PC PEAK DEVELOPMENT\n\n**TO:** Acquisitions Team  \n**RE:** TX-25-01483 - Jamie Cornejo (Life Estate)  \n**DATE:** [Current Date]  \n**PROPERTY:** 1530 E. Overton Rd., Dallas, TX 75216-5506\n\n---\n\n## OWNER SITUATION AND DEBT\n\nTarget owner Jamie Cornejo (a/k/a Jaime Cornejo) holds a life estate interest in the subject property located at 1530 E. Overton Rd., Dallas. This is a tax foreclosure case filed 9/15/2025 in 101st District Court under Judge Carl Ginsberg. Cornejo currently remains **unserved** - citation was attempted via personal service but returned unexecuted on 10/24/2025, indicating possible avoidance or vacancy. Co-defendant Refugio S. Ulloa (same address) was successfully served via Rule 106 substitute service, while Henry Alexander Borg, Jr. (remainder interest holder in Burleson) has been served, retained attorney George Walter McCool, and filed an answer on 10/08/2025. The life estate structure creates complexity, as Cornejo''s interest terminates at death, making this a time-sensitive acquisition opportunity before potential natural expiration of the life estate or forced sale.\n\n## TIMELINE ANALYSIS VS. BENCHMARKS\n\nCase TX-25-01483 is currently **1 month** post-filing with no judgment yet entered. Comparing to benchmark HIGH priority case TX-23-00042 (37 months to judgment, 89 days judgment to OOS), this matter is in extremely early stages. The LOW priority benchmark TX-25-00492 shows 14 months to judgment for simpler cases. **Critical factor:** Borg''s answer filing will likely extend timeline significantly as this creates contested litigation. However, Cornejo''s unserved status may result in default judgment against the life estate interest within 6-9 months if service is eventually perfected via publication. The attorney involvement by one defendant signals sophisticated opposition, suggesting this case will trend closer to the 24-37 month timeline rather than the 14-month baseline.\n\n## ACQUISITION STRATEGY AND OFFER\n\n**Primary approach:** Door-knock campaign at 1530 E. Overton Rd. within next 14 days, targeting weekday evenings (6-8 PM) and Saturday mornings. Given unexecuted service, owner may be present but avoiding process servers - a non-threatening acquisition representative may gain access. **Offer range:** $8,500-$15,000 for life estate release, positioning as','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-05T22:35:40.179856','2026-07-09 05:11:33','2026-07-05T23:26:39.123919',1,'individual','high','','{"account_number": "00000302749000000", "market_value": 155260, "land_value": 95000, "improvement_value": 60260, "estimated_annual_taxes": 3457.19, "year_built": 1935, "effective_year_built": 1935, "actual_age": 91, "building_class": "04", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation": "POST",