ent | Tax Foreclosure Analysis**\n**Case:** TX-26-01379 | **Property:** 4227 York St., Dallas, TX 75210-1741\n**Prepared by:** Senior Acquisitions Analyst | **Date:** July 2026\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is a **land play, not a structure play.** The 1947-built, 1,077 sq/ft single-family structure carries a **60% depreciation factor per DCAD**, placing it near the terminal end of its economic life. At that depreciation level, the improvement contributes diminishing appraised value relative to the underlying lot in the 75210 zip, and any buyer rehabilitating the structure would be fighting a losing cost-basis battle on a sub-1,100 sq/ft footprint. The DCAD market value of **$143,320** almost certainly reflects land-led valuation in a corridor where Dallas infill and teardown activity has accelerated — the structure itself is likely worth $20,000–$30,000 in contributory value at best, meaning the land component is carrying $110,000–$120,000 of that assessed figure. No homestead exemption is on record, confirming this property is **non-owner-occupied** — either a rental, vacant, or simply abandoned by the ownership chain. The deed transferred on **6/22/2020** to **Felicia Denise Taylor (100% ownership)**, who has a known California address at 7930 Valencia Ct., Highland, CA 92346. The payment history tells a fractured story: **Ruby Faye Brown** last paid in **2006**, suggesting she was the long-prior owner or a family member; **Felicia D. Taylor** paid **2021 and 2022** after acquiring title in mid-2020, indicating initial engagement followed by abandonment; then **Howard Taylor** paid **2025** (likely a family member attempting to preserve the asset), before the 2022–2025 delinquency stack accumulated to trigger this filing. This is a **classic absentee family-owned distressed asset** — out-of-state titleholder, partial family intervention, no homestead protection, and a structure that is objectively at or beyond functional obsolescence. The presence of **Mesquite NF SNF, LLC** and its unknown shareholders as a named defendant warrants title scrutiny — this entity may hold a lien, lease interest, or prior contractual claim against the property that will survive foreclosure unless properly adjudicated.\n\n---\n\n## ¶2 — FINANCIAL','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-07T12:38:57.446838','2026-07-09 05:04:52','2026-07-08T19:59:33.470547',1,'individual','high','Being Lot Eight (8) Block ''B''/4473 HG Wall''s Subdivision, an addition in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Warranty Deed recorded as Volume 468, Page 0416 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas','{"account_number": "00000324892000000", "market_value": 143320, "land_value": 70000, "improvement_value": 73320, "estimated_annual_taxes": 3190.52, "year_built": 1947, "effective_year_built": 1947, "actual_age": 79, "building_class": "04", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation": "PIER AND BEAM", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": 1077, "total_area_sqft": 1077, "bedrooms": 2, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": 60, "desirability": "FAIR", "air_condition": "WINDOW", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": null, "zoning": "PLANNED DEVELOPMENT DISTRICT", "lot_frontage_ft": 53, "lot_depth_ft": 109, "lot_area_sqft": 5310.0, "land_unit_price": 70000.0, "legal_description": "1: WALLS H G 2: BLK B/4773 LT 8 3: 4: INT202000160970 DOD10302019 CO-DC 5: 4473 00B 00800 1004473 00B Deed Transfer Date: 6/22/2020", "owners": [{"name": "TAYLOR FELICIA D", "pct": 100}], "deed_transfer_date": "6/22/2020", "exemptions": "None", "no_homestead": true, "tax_rates": [], "current_tax_balance": 11437.29, "current_levy": 2658.79, "prior_year_due": 9552.09, "payment_history": [{"date": "2026-06-17", "amount": 1000.0, "tax_year": "2022", "payer": "FELICIA D TAYLOR"}, {"date": "2026-05-07", "amount": 1500.0, "tax_year": "2025", "payer": "HOWARD TAYLOR"}, {"date": "2022-01-29", 