g\n**Subject Property:** 1000 W Crosby Rd, Carrollton, TX 75006\n**Prepared By:** Acquisitions Desk | Date: July 2026\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ CRITICAL FLAG — READ BEFORE ANALYSIS\n\n**This is NOT a real property tax foreclosure.** The legal description on file is unambiguous: this case targets **business personal property (BPP)** — inventory, equipment, vehicles, machinery, fixtures, and trade goods belonging to Texas Granite & Tile Co. There is **no deed, no land, no structure** being foreclosed. DCAD account #99071031164000000 is a BPP account, not a real property parcel. The "$100,730 market value" reflects an assessed value of **tangible business assets**, not land or improvements. The homestead exemption notation in the intelligence data appears to be a data artifact or system crossover error — a Texas corporation cannot hold a homestead exemption, and this address is a commercial suite (Ste. 300 at 1015 N I-35 is the registered agent address, not a residential property). **PC Peak Development should not underwrite this case as a real estate acquisition.** Full analysis follows for due diligence documentation and disposition decision.\n\n---\n\n## PARAGRAPH 1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\n**This is a business personal property play, not a land or structure play — full stop.** DCAD account #99071031164000000 carries a $100,730 assessed market value attributed entirely to the personal property of Texas Granite & Tile Co., a Texas corporation. There are zero improvement or land value line items because there is no real property attached to this account. The subject address — 1000 W Crosby Rd, Carrollton, TX 75006 — is almost certainly the business''s operating or former operating location in the Valwood Industrial corridor of Carrollton, a dense light-industrial and commercial district near I-35E. The Valwood Improvement Authority appearing as a taxing entity confirms the property sits within that special assessment district, which exclusively covers industrial/commercial parcels. The fact that DCAD data returns blank fields for year built, square footage, exterior type, and depreciation percentage is entirely consistent with a BPP account — those fields are real property fields. The "homestead exemption: YES" flag in the intelligence pull is a known data crossover error that sometimes occurs when a BPP account shares an address range with a','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-07T12:39:54.566900','2026-07-09 05:14:23','2026-07-08T20:00:37.163564',1,'individual','high','ALL THE MONEY, NOTES, BONDS, STOCKS, CREDITS, STOCK OF GOODS, WARES, MERCHANDISE, SUPPLIES, FIXTURES, TOOLS, MACHINERY, EQUIPMENT, AUTOMOBILES, TRUCKS, AND/OR OTHER MOTOR VEHICLES, AIRCRAFT, VESSELS, FURNITURE, FURNISHINGS, (INCLUDING COMPUTERS, TELECOMMUNICATIONS AND OTHER ELECTRICAL EQUIPMENT) AND SUPPLIES USED IN THE CONDUCT OF BUSINESS, INCLUDING ALL PERSONAL PROPERTY DESCRIBED BELOW: PERSONAL PROPERTY TEXAS GRANITE & TILE CO.','{"account_number": "99071031164000000", "market_value": 100730, "land_value": 0, "improvement_value": 100730, "estimated_annual_taxes": 0.0, "year_built": null, "effective_year_built": null, "actual_age": null, "building_class": "", "construction_type": "", "foundation": "", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": null, "total_area_sqft": null, "bedrooms": null, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": null, "desirability": "", "air_condition": "", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": null, "zoning": "", "lot_frontage_ft": null, "lot_depth_ft": null, "lot_area_sqft": null, "land_unit_price": null, "legal_description": "1: TEXAS GRANITE & TILE CO 2: 3: 4: 5: Deed Transfer Date:", "owners": [{"name": "TEXAS GRANITE & TILE CO", "pct": 100}], "deed_transfer_date": "", "exemptions": "City\tSchool\tCounty\tCollege\tHospital\tSpecial District", "no_homestead": false, "tax_rates": [{"entity": "DALLAS COUNTY\tDALLAS COLLEGE\tPARKLAND HOSPITAL\tVALWOOD IMPROVEMENT AUTHORITY\nB