C Peak Development | Internal Use Only\n**Case:** TX-26-01374 | **Property:** 3203 Utah Ave., Dallas, TX 75216 | **Date:** July 2026\n**Analyst:** Senior Acquisitions | **Priority:** HIGH | **Distress Score:** 7/10 — CRITICAL\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThe subject property at 3203 Utah Ave. is a 1,358 sq ft residential structure built in 1948, now 78 years old and carrying a 50% depreciation rating per DCAD — placing this asset firmly in late economic life territory. DCAD pegs total market value at **$194,810**, but the composition of that value is the critical question: on a Trinity Heights Annex lot, the land itself is likely carrying a disproportionate share of that assessed figure. A 78-year-old, 50% depreciated wood-frame structure in the 75216 zip code is not the value driver here — **this is fundamentally a land play with a teardown-or-rehab decision overlay.** The improvement value likely sits in the $60,000–$80,000 range against land value approaching $110,000–$130,000, which means any buyer who underwrites this as a turnkey rehab is mispricing the risk. The structure likely requires $40,000–$65,000 minimum in capital to be rentable at market rates, and that''s before addressing foundation issues common to late-1940s Dallas slab and pier-and-beam stock in this corridor.\n\nOn ownership, the DCAD record reflects **RIVERS MARTHA at 100% ownership**, with deed transfer recorded **June 8, 2000** — meaning this asset has been held 26 years under the current ownership chain. However, the lawsuit names four defendants: **Edward Brown Sr., Eva Mae Brown, Martha Rivers, and John Will Brown** — a multi-generational family ownership structure almost certainly arising from an **estate situation or informal title transfer** that was never properly probated or conveyed. The deed recorded in Volume 72144, Page 0081 of Dallas County Deed Records under a Special Warranty Deed suggests Martha Rivers acquired through a family transaction, but the continued inclusion of the Brown family members as defendants indicates LGBS/Linebarger identified competing or residual ownership interests — possibly heirs who never formally released interest. Payment history sharpens this picture materially: **Texas Tax Solution II LLC paid 2019** (a tax lender intervention, meaning the property was already delinquent as of 2018–2019), and **Rivers Martha','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-07T12:42:53.818902','2026-07-09 05:04:52','2026-07-08T20:55:11.733590',1,'individual','high','Being Lot 13, in Block 21/5999 of Trinity Heights Annex, an addition in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Special Warranty Deed recorded in Volume 72144 Page 0081 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas.','{"account_number": "00000477631000000", "market_value": 194810, "land_value": 85000, "improvement_value": 109810, "estimated_annual_taxes": 4337.85, "year_built": 1948, "effective_year_built": 1948, "actual_age": 78, "building_class": "04", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation": "PIER AND BEAM", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": 1358, "total_area_sqft": 1358, "bedrooms": 3, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": 50, "desirability": "AVERAGE", "air_condition": "WINDOW", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": null, "zoning": "SINGLE FAMILY 7500 SQFT", "lot_frontage_ft": 60, "lot_depth_ft": 173, "lot_area_sqft": 10152.0, "land_unit_price": 85000.0, "legal_description": "1: TRINITY HEIGHTS ANNEX 2: BLK 21/5999 LT 13 3: 4: VOL2000113/3422 DD05032000 CO-DC 5: 5999 021 01300 4DA5999 021 Deed Transfer Date: 6/8/2000", "owners": [{"name": "RIVERS MARTHA", "pct": 100}], "deed_transfer_date": "6/8/2000", "exemptions": "None", "no_homestead": true, "tax_rates": [], "current_tax_balance": 19175.83, "current_levy": 4337.86, "prior_year_due": 13033.41, "payment_history": [{"date": "2023-04-18", "amount": 4486.87, "tax_year": "2022", "payer": "RIVERS MARTHA"}, {"