INSERT INTO cases VALUES(43,'TX-26-00879','116th District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2026-05-01','OPEN','TAX DELINQUENCY','Armandina De La Rocha, as Co-Trustee of the Armandina and Jose De La Rocha Revocable Trust','[{"name": "Armandina De La Rocha, as Co-Trustee of the Armandina and Jose De La Rocha Revocable Trust", "address": "101 S. Montclair Ave., Dallas, TX 75208", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "Private Process Server", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Unexecuted citation returned 06/01/2026"}, {"name": "Jose De La Rocha, as Co-Trustee of the Armandina and Jose De La Rocha Revocable Trust", "address": "101 S. Montclair Ave., Dallas, TX 75208", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "Private Process Server", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Unexecuted citation returned 06/01/2026"}, {"name": "The United States of America", "address": "Nancy E. Larson, United States Attorney, 1100 Commerce Street, Third Floor, Dallas, TX 75242; and Attorney General for the United States, Tenth and Constitution, Washington, DC 20430", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "Private Process Server", "isInRemOnly": true, "notes": "Executed citation returned 06/09/2026; federal tax liens by IRS filed 08/18/2014 (Doc. 201400208822), 01/21/2015 (Doc. 201500015170), 02/26/2015 (Doc. 201500047071) against Armandina and Jose De La Rocha"}]','5815 W. Jefferson Blvd., Dallas, TX 75211-7042',NULL,'00000806512000100','LGBS (Linebarger)','Ashly S. Atkins',19569.63000000000008,2022,'[2022, 2023, 2024, 2025]',3,0,0,'[{"suitNo": "TX-12-31071", "style": "DALLAS COUNTY, ET AL VS. JOSE E. DE LA ROCHA, ET AL", "court": "160th District Court, Dallas County, Texas"}]',0,0,0,'Two primary defendants (Armandina De La Rocha and Jose De La Rocha) remain unserved as of 06/01/2026; unexecuted citations returned for both. Only the United States of America (In Rem Only) has been served.','high',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,0,'2027-01-19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 1258.65, "penaltyInterest": 596.14, "total": 1854.79}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 1259.63, "penaltyInterest": 602.21, "total": 1861.84}, {"entity": "Dallas College", "taxAmt": 629.87, "penaltyInterest": 300.57, "total": 930.44}, {"entity": "Dallas County School Equalization Fund", "taxAmt": 3.83, "penaltyInterest": 3.15, "total": 6.98}, {"entity": "Dallas Independent School District", "taxAmt": 5914.11, "penaltyInterest": 2832.77, "total": 8746.88}, {"entity": "City of Dallas", "taxAmt": 4172.82, "penaltyInterest": 1995.88, "total": 6168.7}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Internal Use Only**\n**Case:** TX-26-00879 | **Property:** 5815 W. Jefferson Blvd., Dallas, TX 75211\n**Prepared By:** Acquisitions Analyst | **Date:** June 2026\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThe subject property at 5815 W. Jefferson Blvd. sits on **0.5779 acres** in the Enoch Horton Survey (Block 8344, Tract 3.1) in the Oak Cliff/West Jefferson corridor of Dallas 75211 — a transitional commercial-residential strip with active redevelopment pressure from the Jefferson Boulevard corridor revitalization. At **$194,900 DCAD market value** on a half-acre lot, this immediately flags as a **land play, not a structure play**. The DCAD data is critically incomplete — year built, square footage, and exterior construction are all blank, which typically indicates either an unimproved tract, a structure of negligible improvement value, or a data suppression anomaly on a recently transferred parcel. The absence of improvement detail combined with the lot size strongly suggests the land itself is the asset. For context, comparable half-acre commercial-adjacent lots on W. Jefferson are trading in the **$8–$12/sqft range** ($252K–$378K), meaning DCAD''s $194,900 valuation may actually be **under-assessed**, which benefits a buyer at foreclosure but compresses the distress discount. Ownership history is telling: the property was held under the **Armandina and Jose De La Rocha Revocable Trust**, with a deed transfer recorded **January 7, 2025** (Instrument No. 202500003861). This is a 2002-era acquisition (DD 09/27/2002, Vol. 2002198/7695) held for over 22 years before that transfer event. The trust structure is a red flag for complexity — revocable living trusts in Texas do not shield assets from tax foreclosure, but they do require **both co-trustees** (Armandina and Jose) to execute any conveyance. The payment history shows Armandina was the active payor through 2022–2025, while Jose''s last recorded payment was 2022, suggesting possible separation of financial responsibilities or Jose''s diminished involvement. The January 2025 deed transfer — occurring just four months before the May 2026 suit filing — warrants immediate title investigation: was this a conveyance **out of** the trust, or a re-recording event? If they conve','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-07T22:47:42.890968','2026-07-09 05:04:53','2026-07-08T19:25:16.567155',1,'individual','high','Being a tract of land situated in the Enoch Horton Survey, Abstract No. 613, and being part of the City Block No. 8344 in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Warranty Deed recorded as Instrument Number 202500003861 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas. BLK 8344 TR 3.1 ACS 0.5779 VOL 2002198/7695 DD 09272002 CO-DC 8433','{"account_number": "00000806512000100", "market_value": 194900, "land_value": 100690, "improvement_value": 94210, "estimated_annual_taxes": 4339.86, "year_built": null, "effective_year_built": null, "actual_age": null, "building_class": "", "construction_type": "", "foundation": "", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": null, "total_area_sqft": null, "bedrooms": null, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": null, "desirability": "", "air_condition": "", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": null, "zoning": "COMMERCIAL S