 sq ft, this structure sits well below the Dallas metro average of ~1,800 sq ft for SFR and is economically obsolete for most retail buyer profiles. DCAD''s total market value of **$176,860** on a sub-800 sq ft lot in the 75227 zip (Southeast Dallas / Urbandale Addition corridor) suggests the land itself is absorbing the majority of that valuation — a classic infill teardown or redevelopment scenario. The improvement-to-land value ratio warrants confirmation via DCAD''s breakdown, but the combination of age, size, and depreciation rate signals that any investor paying for this asset is paying for **dirt and position, not sticks**. The absence of a homestead exemption is a critical behavioral flag: Molina Flores is **not living here**. This is either a rental, a vacant property, or an asset she has emotionally and financially disengaged from. The deed transfer recorded **June 3, 2011** (Instrument No. 201100141602) shows she has held this property for 15 years. Prior to her ownership, **MATAMOROS TROPIC** held the asset and paid taxes through 2010 — a likely predecessor owner or related party from whom she acquired it. Her own payment history shows **compliance through 2021 and 2022**, meaning delinquency didn''t begin until tax year 2022 — this is not a chronic tax evader, but someone whose financial situation or relationship to the property **materially changed around 2022-2023**. That pivot point — a job loss, a relocation, a family event — is your opening in the conversation. No prior related suits exist, no estate/heir complications, single defendant, clean title chain. This is a straightforward individual owner situation with low legal complexity.\n\n---\n\n## ¶2 — FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nAt filing on **June','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-07T22:59:20.948945','2026-07-09 05:04:54','2026-07-08T20:42:56.789121',1,'individual','high','Being Lot 8, in Block B/5828, of Urbandale Addition No. 1, an addition in the City of Dallas, Dallas 