t 6, Block 44A/5845 of the Kessler Heights Addition No. 3 — a recorded plat in an area of Dallas (75216) that has seen significant infill and redevelopment pressure. At 71 years of age with DCAD recording **50% physical depreciation**, this structure is functionally at or near the end of its economic life. The improvement-to-land value ratio signals this clearly: with a total market value of $180,620 on an 812 sqft structure, a significant portion of that assessed value is being carried by the **lot itself**, not the building. A 50%-depreciated, sub-900 sqft 1955 frame structure in this zip code is not a candidate for conventional renovation financing — it''s a tear-down or heavy-lift cash deal. The **absence of a homestead exemption** is one of the most operationally important data points in this file: Linda Washington Lott is **not living at 2428 52nd Street**. Her listed address of record is 4000 E. Renner Rd., Apt. 1413, Richardson, TX 75082 — a full 18 miles from the subject property. The deed transfer recorded in **Volume 74195, Page 1435** dates to **October 7, 1974** — over 51 years of ownership under various name iterations (Linda Ann Shaw, Linda Washington, Linda Lott, Linda W. Lott, Linda Washington Lott). This long-tenure absentee owner profile is a high-conversion archetype: the asset is almost certainly not generating income that covers carrying costs, emotional attachment may be offset by the burden of management from Richardson, and the tax delinquency pattern confirms she is no longer actively managing this asset. The prior related suit **TX-11-30416** indicates this is not the first time this property has entered the foreclosure pipeline — a repeat delinquency pattern that materially increases owner motivation and reduces the likelihood of a lender payoff or family intervention.\n\n---\n\n## ¶2 — FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nAt filing on **June 2, 2026**, the total tax debt was certified at **$','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-