024, 2025]',8,1,0,'[{"suitNo": "TX-23-01384", "style": "DALLAS COUNTY, ETAL VS. MARION F. MCCORD, ETAL", "court": "68th District Court", "county": "Dallas County, Texas"}]',1,0,0,'Two defendants (Marion F. McCord and F.B. McCord, Sr.) have unknown addresses requiring Citation by Posting. All 8 defendants currently unserved as of filing. Attorney Ad Litem appointed 06/30/2026. Property titled to McCord Marion F. Est. Of & Etal suggesting estate/heir situation.','high',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,0,'2027-02-15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 2824.07, "penaltyInterest": 2575.41, "total": 5399.48}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 3028.86, "penaltyInterest": 2837.63, "total": 5866.49}, {"entity": "Dallas College", "taxAmt": 1439.43, "penaltyInterest": 1319.77, "total": 2759.2}, {"entity": "Dallas County School Equalization Fund", "taxAmt": 68.44, "penaltyInterest": 81.77, "total": 150.21}, {"entity": "Dallas Independent School District", "taxAmt": 14374.57, "penaltyInterest": 13475.08, "total": 27849.65}, {"entity": "City of Hutchins", "taxAmt": 6787.82, "penaltyInterest": 5425.56, "total": 12213.38}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Texas Tax Foreclosure Division**\n**Case:** TX-26-01194 | **Property:** 740 Crockett St., Hutchins, TX 75141\n**Prepared:** July 2026 | **Analyst:** Senior Acquisitions | **Priority Rating:** HIGH\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\n740 Crockett Street is a 1,068-square-foot single-family structure built in 1960, now 66 years old and carrying a 50% depreciation factor per DCAD assessment methodology. At $197,050 total market value, the improvement component is being discounted heavily by the county''s own model — this signals a structure approaching functional obsolescence, not a rehabbed asset. For context, DCAD''s land-to-improvement ratio on aging Hutchins residential parcels typically runs 30–40% land value; at $197,050 market value with 50% depreciation applied to the structure, the implied improvement value is likely in the $80,000–$95,000 range with land carrying $100,000–$120,000 of the total. **This is fundamentally a land play.** Hutchins is a dense industrial and logistics corridor along I-45 south of Dallas, and a sub-$200K residential lot on a named street in that zip presents more value as a cleared site or assemblage candidate than as a structure rehabilitation project. The exterior condition is unlisted in DCAD, which in our experience indicates the property was either not inspected recently or the condition was not codeable — both are red flags for physical deterioration. No homestead exemption on record confirms the property is **not owner-occupied** and almost certainly vacant or tenant-neglected.\n\nOwnership is held as **"MCCORD MARION F EST OF & ET AL"** — an estate designation that has never been formally resolved through probate, at least not reflected in DCAD. The deed transfer date of **8/27/1992** means this title has sat dormant for 34 years. The "ET AL" in the ownership record explains the cascade of in rem defendants: **Faye M. McQueen, F.B. McCord Jr., Ronnie G. McCord, Sherry A. Soukup, Danny G. McCord, Marion Stanislawski, and F.B. McCord Sr.** — all presumptive heirs of Marion F. McCord (deceased). This is a classic **multi-heir intestate estate scenario** where no single party has control, motivation, or legal authority to act unilaterally. The payment history','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-07T23:27:13.506435','2026-07-09 05:04:55','2026-07-08T20:51:23.177434',1,'individual','high','Being Lot 9 in Block B, Second Section of Hutchins Heights Addition, an addition in the City of Hutchins, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Warranty Deed recorded in Volume 5309 Page 525 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas','{"account_number": "30011500020090000", "market_value": 197050, "land_value": 65000, "improvement_value": 132050, "estimated_a