**PC Peak Development | Dallas Acquisitions Desk**\n**Case:** TX-26-01386 | **Property:** 4921 Sunnyvale St., Dallas, TX 75223\n**Date:** July 2026 | **Analyst:** Senior Acquisitions\n**Distress Score:** 11/CRITICAL | **Classification:** PRIORITY PURSUIT\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is a **land play with a demolition scenario**, not a structure play. The subject is a 1935-vintage, 876 sqft single-family structure in Lakewood Heights (Blk 10/5393, Lt 17) carrying a 50% depreciation factor on DCAD records — meaning DCAD itself is acknowledging the structure has consumed roughly half its economic utility. At 91 years old, the mechanical systems (electrical, plumbing, HVAC, foundation) are statistically at or past end-of-life. The improvement-to-land value split on a $155,260 total market value in the 75223 zip code — which has seen aggressive infill development pressure from East Dallas — almost certainly skews heavily toward land value. Lakewood Heights lots are commanding premium pricing as teardown/infill candidates, and a 50%-depreciated 876 sqft structure adds negligible functional value. **This asset should be underwritten as a cleared lot play.** The ownership picture is fractured and deeply irregular: DCAD currently shows a **life estate / remainder interest structure** — Jamie Cornejo (life estate + 16%), Refugio Ulloa (16%), and Cirilo Uyoa (68%) — yet the deed transfer date is **July 24, 2025**, just 348 days before the lawsuit was filed. That recent conveyance is a serious red flag: the defendants named in the tax suit are **Teresa Marie Hunt** and **Jack D. Hunt**, with a third party **Tracy Tomlin** at a Mesquite address (3802 Bonnywood Dr.), meaning DCAD ownership and court-named defendants are misaligned. Prior payment history shows at least three different payer identities — Rosa Setina (2020), Borg Jewell Dean (2019), Rosa Petina (2017) — suggesting this property has cycled through informal arrangements, possible owner-financing, or deed-in-lieu transfers without clean title work. The Hunt defendants are likely the immediately preceding owners or contract-for-deed holders whose interest was either conveyed or extinguished by the July 2025 deed, yet they remain legally liable for the delinquency period 2021','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-08T19:55:38.461542','2026-07-10T07:05:22.067495','2026-07-10T07:05:22.067495',1,'individual','high','LAKEWOOD HEIGHTS, BLK 10/5393, LT 17','{"account_number": "00000302749000000", "market_value": 155260, "land_value": 95000, "improvement_value": 60260, "estimated_annual_taxes": 3457.19, "year_built": 1935, "effective_year_built": 1935, "actual_age": 91, "building_class": "04", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation": "POST", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": 876, "total_area_sqft": 876, "bedrooms": 2, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": 50, "desirability": "AVERAGE", "air_condition": "WINDOW", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": 320, "zoning": "SINGLE FAMILY 7500 SQFT", "lot_frontage_ft": 50, "lot_depth_ft": 170, "lot_area_sqft": 8731.0, "land_unit_price": 95000.0, "legal_description": "1: LIBERTY HEIGHTS 2: BLK 27/4076 LT 2 3: 4: INT202500153512 DD07212025 CO-DC 5: 4076 027 00200 2004076 027 Deed Transfer Date: 7/24/2025", "owners": [{"name": "CORNEJO JAMIE LIFE ESTATE &", "pct": 16}, {"name": "ULLOA REFUGIO &", "pct": 16}, {"name": "UYOA CIRILO &", "pct": 68}], "deed_transfer_date": "7/24/2025", "exemptions": "None", "no_homestead": true, "tax_rates": [], "current_tax_balance": 22144.85, "current_levy": 3281.8, "prior_year_due": 17497.81, "payment_history": [{"date": "2021-01-12", "amount": 666.51, "tax_year": "2020", "payer": "ROSA SETINA"}, {"date": "2021-01-12", "amount": 1000.0, "tax_year": "2020", "payer": "ROSA SETINA"}, {"date": "2020-01-27", "amount": 1077.03, "tax_year": "2019", "payer": "BORG JEWELL DEAN"}, {"date": "2019-01-15", "amount": 751.15, "tax_y