 OWNER SITUATION\n\nThe subject property is a 2,004 SF single-family structure on Lot 17 and the West 15'' of Lot 18, Block 11/6317, Tanglewood Subdivision, built in **1962 and carrying a 50% depreciation load** per DCAD''s own assessment model — meaning the structure itself is functionally at or near the terminal end of its economic life by conventional appraisal standards. At $298,710 DCAD market value with a 64-year-old frame structure, the critical question is whether the land is doing the heavy lifting here. Dallas 75217 is an infill corridor where teardown-and-rebuild economics are increasingly viable, and a lot configuration of Lot 17 plus a 15-foot strip of Lot 18 likely yields a **wider-than-standard lot footprint**, which adds disproportionate land value and strengthens the case for a land-play or at minimum a gut-rehab-to-rental strategy rather than a cosmetic flip. The absence of a homestead exemption is a loud signal: **Stephen and Charlotte Laughlin are not living at 8422 Foxwood Ln.** The mailing address of record for both defendants is **7255 Eccles Dr., Dallas, TX 75227** — a separate Dallas address approximately 3 miles southwest — confirming this is a non-owner-occupied investment or inherited asset sitting idle. The deed transfer recorded in **October 1984** means the Laughlins have held this property for roughly 42 years, suggesting either long-term rental fatigue, inherited estate complications, or simple neglect of a legacy asset. The payment history is the most operationally valuable intelligence in this file: **Charlotte Laughlin** paid 2023; **Christina Laughlin** paid 2022; **Charlotte Locklin** (likely same person, name variation or remarriage artifact) paid 2021; **Laughlin Stephen ETAL** paid 2018. The name fragmentation across four tax receipts — four different name variants over five payment cycles — signals a disorganized ownership structure, possible family dispute over the asset, or a situation where multiple parties have been kicking the can. The 2024 and 2025','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-08T19:57:28.338823','2026-07-09 05:04:57','2026-07-08T19:57:28.338823',1,'individual','high','Being Lot 17 and the West 15'' of Lot 18, in Block 11/6317, Tanglewood Subdivision, 2nd Installment, an Addition in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Warranty Deed recorded in Volume 84209 Page 5149 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas','{"account_number": "00000564967000000", "market_value": 298710, "land_value": 77000, "improvement_value": 221710, "estimated_annual_taxes": 4936.35, "year_built": 1962, "effective_year_built": 1962, "actual_age": 64, "building_class": "14", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation": "PIER AND BEAM", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": 2004, "total_area_sqft": 2004, "bedrooms": 4, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": 50, "desirability": "AVERAGE", "air_condition": "CENTRAL FULL", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": 440, "zoning": "SINGLE FAMILY 7500 SQFT", "lot_frontage_ft": 75, "lot_depth_ft": 125, "lot_area_sqft": 9530.0, "land_unit_price": 70000.0, "legal_description": "1: TANGLEWOOD REV 2: LOT 17 & W 15FT LOT 18 3: FOXWOOD LANE 4: VOL84209 PG5149 CO-DALLAS 5: 6317 011 017 3006317 011 Deed Transfer Date: 10/23/1984", "owners": [{"name": "LAUGHLIN STEPHEN & CHARLOTTE", "pct": 100}], "deed_transfer_date": "10/23/1984", "exemptions": "None", "no_homestead": true, "tax_rates": [], "current_tax_balance": 11174.38, "current_levy": 4113.62, "prior_year_due": 5349.49, "payment_history": [{"date": "2025-05-16", "amount": 1000.0, "tax_year": "2023", "payer": "CHARLOTTE LAUGHLIN"}, {"date": "2023-06-30", "amount": 3274.13, "tax_year": "2022", "payer": "CHRISTINA LAUGHLIN"}, {"date": "2023-01-30", "amount": 2000.0, "tax_year": "2021, 2022", "payer": "CHARLOTTE LAUGHLIN"}, {"date": "2022-10-31", "amount": 600.0, "tax_year": "2021", "payer": "CHARLOTTE LOCKLIN"}, {"date": "20